# =============================================================================
# Product — CATEGORY LIST probes — GET /api/v1/categories (ADMIN or any store admin)
# =============================================================================
# How to run:
#   1. Start the backend: `docker compose up -d --build` — http://localhost:4000
#   2. Click the "Send Request" CodeLens above any request below.
#
# Prerequisites (admin persona):
#   Signup admin@devtunde.com with Password123! once, then promote in MySQL:
#     update users set role = 'ROLE_ADMIN' where email = 'admin@devtunde.com';
#
# Notes:
#   - Run top-to-bottom on first use. This file walks one persona from
#     "plain user" to "store admin" to prove the isStoreAdmin read gate.
#   - All data is FAKE (devtunde.com emails, Nigerian numbers).
#   - The automated suite: ProductApiTests (src/test/java).
#   - Tokens expire after 15 MINUTES — re-send the setup requests from
#     the top (they mint fresh captures anyway), then continue.
#   - Response captures are SESSION-SCOPED: closing/reopening this file or VS Code clears them. If a request errors with "No value is resolved" or the URL carries raw template text, re-send the setup requests from the top.
#   - Re-running is SAFE: the reader persona, her store, and the vocabulary
#     category are all minted fresh via {{$timestamp}} each run — one store
#     per admin is a committed rule, so the reader must be fresh like her
#     store (she seeds it at request 8).
#   - Expected codes: 200 list, 401 no/garbage token, 403 plain user.
# =============================================================================

@categoryUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/categories
@storeUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/stores
@authUrl = http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth

### 1 — Setup: login the admin persona
# Expected: 200
# @name adminLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2 — List categories as the chain admin
# Expected: 200 — array of {publicId, name, createdAt, updatedAt}
GET {{categoryUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 3 — No Authorization header
# Expected: 401
GET {{categoryUrl}}

### 4 — Garbage token
# Expected: 401
GET {{categoryUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-jwt

### 5 — Setup: signup the reader persona (fresh every run, starts as a plain user)
# Expected: 201 — a brand-new persona each run
# @name readerSignup
POST {{authUrl}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Catalog Reader",
  "email": "probe-reader-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348031110002"
}

### 6 — Setup: login the reader persona
# Expected: 200
# @name readerLogin
POST {{authUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{readerSignup.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 7 — List as a plain user (no store, not admin)
# Expected: 403 — the read gate is chain admin OR any store admin
GET {{categoryUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{readerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 8 — Setup: admin creates a store, making the reader a STORE ADMIN
# Expected: 201
# @name readerStore
POST {{storeUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "brand": "Reader Home Store {{$timestamp}}",
  "description": "Store for the category reader persona",
  "storeType": "BRANCH",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{readerLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "1 Reader Street, Lagos",
    "phone": "08012345678",
    "email": "reader-home-store-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 9 — List again — same person, now a store admin
# Expected: 200 — the isStoreAdmin gate opens: role is still ROLE_USER,
# but "administers any store" is a data fact, not a role
GET {{categoryUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{readerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 10 — Setup: admin adds a fresh category for the reader to find
# Expected: 201
# @name readerVocabulary
POST {{categoryUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "name": "Reader Vocabulary {{$timestamp}}"
}

### 11 — Reader lists again — eyeball the minted "Reader Vocabulary …" name
# Expected: 200
GET {{categoryUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{readerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
